# The Vercel CLI uploads the working directory and deliberately does NOT read
# .gitignore -- it honours only this file plus a hardcoded list. That list
# covers `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, but not the dotless `env.local` or a
# timestamped backup like `.env.local.bak-qa-20260921`, and those hold the
# service-role key, the cron secrets and a Cloudflare API token. Every one of
# them is invisible to `git status` because .gitignore already excludes it, so
# nothing else would have stopped them being shipped into a deployment.
#
# Runtime configuration on Vercel comes from the project's environment
# variables, never from a file in the tree, so excluding all of these is safe.
env.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local tooling state and build output.
.vercel
.next
node_modules
supabase/.temp
supabase/.branches
.pi
.pi-tasks
